
# --- playbook commit template (docs/12 2, docs/16 4.1) ---
# Conventional Commits, written in English:
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
# type:  feat | fix | chore | docs | refactor | test | perf | ci | build | style | revert | infra
# scope: the package, app or layer the change belongs to (web | api | shared | infra | ci ...)
# subject: imperative mood, <= ~72 chars, no trailing period ("add x", not "added x")
#
# Body (optional): explain the WHY (not the how), wrap at ~72 cols.
#
# Rules:
# - Author is nerdkim. Keep the sanctioned co-author trailer below; never add any
#   OTHER co-author (e.g. Claude) or a generated signature.
# - No forbidden unicode (em dash / en dash / bullet ...); ASCII only (docs/16 2.1).
# - Documents and replies are Korean; code, comments, commit and PR are English (docs/16 4.1).
#
# `git commit -m` never renders this template, so an agent that commits with -m must add the
# trailer itself. Rule M7 of harness/check-commit-messages.sh reports its absence.

Co-Authored-By: mikdren <bot-sidekick@nerd.kim>
